Here's a clean implementation with the search icon inside the input on the right side:

```jsx
import { useState } from "react";

const SearchInput = () => {
  const [value, setValue] = useState("");

  const handleSearch = () => {
    if (value.trim()) {
      console.log("Searching for:", value);
      // Your search logic here
    }
  };

  const handleKeyDown = (e) => {
    if (e.key === "Enter") {
      handleSearch();
    }
  };

  return (
    <div style={{ position: "relative", display: "inline-block" }}>
      <input
        type="text"
        value={value}
        onChange={(e) => setValue(e.target.value)}
        onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}
        placeholder="Search..."
        style={{
          padding: "8px 40px 8px 12px",
          border: "1px solid #ccc",
          borderRadius: "8px",
          fontSize: "16px",
          outline: "none",
          width: "250px",
        }}
      />

      {/* Search Icon */}
      <svg
        onClick={handleSearch}
        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
        width="20"
        height="20"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="#888"
        strokeWidth="2"
        strokeLinecap="round"
        strokeLinejoin="round"
        style={{
          position: "absolute",
          right: "10px",
          top: "50%",
          transform: "translateY(-50%)",
          cursor: "pointer",
        }}
      >
        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8" />
        <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65" />
      </svg>
    </div>
  );
};

export default SearchInput;
```

### Key points:
- **`position: relative`** on the wrapper div keeps the icon anchored to the input
- **`padding-right: 40px`** on the input prevents text from going under the icon
- **`position: absolute`** + **`right: 10px`** + **`top: 50%`** + **`transform: translateY(-50%)`** centers the icon vertically on the right side
- **`cursor: pointer`** makes it clear the icon is clickable
- The `handleSearch` function is called both on **icon click** and **Enter key press**

Just replace the `console.log` inside `handleSearch` with your own function/logic.

